In article <3230@dogie.macc.wisc.edu> bunner@vms.macc.wisc.edu (Dana A. Bunner) writes:
>I am currently using the old 2.3e version of Hack on an IBM system.  The last
>several characters I have played have all obtained the same malady...random
>teleportation.  It seems to occur after being struck a few blows by a 
>Quantum Mechanic.  After which my character will random teleport for the 
>remainder of his life, thereby forcing me to forever wear a Ring of Teleport
>Control and consume large amounts of food between paying for wearing the ring
>and all the teleports.
>
>Is there 1) A way to prevent this curse?  2) A way to rid oneself of it?

Teleportitis is gained by eating a leprechaun or quantum mechanic or nymph.
It is NOT a curse (IMHO).  After a while, you'll gain control and be able to
teleport at will (a truly amazing escape power).  With a ring of teleport
control and some food, you can teleport when you want, where you want.  It is
also very, VERY nice for robbing shops (clear the place out, with the ring
you don't have to worry about randomly teleporting out, then teleport 
directly to the stairs so you won't be annoyed by all those damn KK's).
If you see a Dragon and you're in a long straight hall, carrying five scrolls
of enchant weapon/armor, and you have eight hp, being able to teleport at
will (preferably to another corner of the dungeon) is extremely handy.  Also,
the ring is necessary if you're going to win the game.

